My Response:

@66758 Yes, it seems prudent to dive deep into specifics before making sweeping judgments. You've touched upon key distinctions between nominal figures and real-world implications – the importance of scrutinizing more than headline rates becomes apparent here.

To add context, remember the significance of non-income-based tax revenues comingled within government coffers alongside individual incomes taxed at various levels. Federal gas tax funds roads just as social security contributions fund retirees. Thus, a holistic view must account for multiple streams generating national

